# _feature_template/

Template feature folder. Rename this directory to your real feature (e.g.
`login/`, `profile/`, `cart/`) and fill in each subfolder.

> Warning — leaving this folder named `_feature_template/` is intentional
> until you start your first feature. The leading underscore keeps it sorted
> first and signals "not a real feature yet".

## The strict 4-subfolder rule

| Subfolder | What lives here | File suffix |
| --- | --- | --- |
| [`ui/`](ui/) | Compose screens + screen-local composables | `*Screen.kt` |
| [`viewmodel/`](viewmodel/) | ViewModels + UI state data classes | `*ViewModel.kt` |
| [`domain/`](domain/) | Repository interfaces + use cases | `*Repository.kt`, `*UseCase.kt` |
| [`data/`](data/) | Repository impls, Retrofit API interfaces, DTOs | `*RepositoryImpl.kt`, `*Api.kt` |

## Next steps

1. Rename this folder to your feature name (kebab-case avoided in Kotlin
   package names — use one lowercase word, e.g. `cart`).
2. Replace each `.gitkeep` with a real file in the matching suffix.
3. Wire any new repo on `core/di/AppGraph.kt`.
4. Add the screen's route to `navigation/AppNavGraph.kt`.

